{
  "message": "I can help with that — but before I access your account I need to verify your identity. Please provide either your user ID, registered email, or your full name, AND provide any two of the following: (1) date of birth (MM/DD/YYYY), (2) registered phone number, (3) registered address. Once you provide those, I’ll verify and then check your Silver Rewards Card cash back details. If you’d prefer not to share these here, I can either walk you through what to check on your statements or transfer you to a human agent — which would you prefer?"
}

{
  "message": "Thanks — I can’t submit those cash-back disputes directly from my side because the knowledge base shows submission is done with the user-facing tool submit_cash_back_dispute_0589 (I’ve already made that tool available to you). I’m sorry for the confusion. Below are exact, copy-paste commands you can run to file both disputes yourself, plus what to expect and next steps I can help with.",
  "how_to_submit_commands": [
    "submit_cash_back_dispute_0589(user_id: \"6680a37184\", transaction_id: \"txn_913d14a20dc5\")  // Amazon $156.78 on 11/05/2025",
    "submit_cash_back_dispute_0589(user_id: \"6680a37184\", transaction_id: \"txn_cfabb609133d\")  // Sushi Kashiba $87.25 on 11/10/2025"
  ],
  "notes_about_submission": "You do not need receipts to start the submission. The dispute tool will create a case for each transaction and should return a case/reference ID after you run it.",
  "expected_timeline_and_outcome": {
    "provisional_credit": "If eligible, provisional credit is typically issued within 10 business days (20 days for new accounts). Eligibility depends on dispute reason and account history.",
    "investigation_completion": "Most investigations are completed within 45 days (some international or complex cases can take up to 90 days).",
    "resolution_and_adjustment": "If the rewards team confirms an undercredit, they will apply the correct rewards adjustment and you’ll receive notification and the case reference will show the outcome."
  },
  "additional_info": {
    "why_this_happens": "Common causes are merchant misclassification, third-party processors, or posting errors — the investigation will verify merchant category and the rewards calculation.",
    "what_i_can_do_now": "I can (pick one):\n  • Walk you step-by-step through running the submit_cash_back_dispute_0589 commands right here.\n  • Transfer you to a human agent who can file the disputes on your behalf (if you prefer).",
    "recommendation": "If you’d like me to guide you, say “Please help me run them now.” If you prefer a human to file them, say “Transfer me” and I’ll initiate the transfer."
  }
}

{
  "message": "Thanks — I checked your dispute records. Here’s what I found and recommended next steps.",
  "amazon_dispute": {
    "transaction_id": "txn_913d14a20dc5",
    "dispute_record_id_found": "dsp_7a3e91b4c2d8",
    "status": "UNDER_REVIEW",
    "submitted_at": "11/10/2025",
    "dispute_reason": "duplicate_charge",
    "contacted_merchant_on_record": true,
    "eligible_for_provisional_credit": true,
    "provisional_credit_given": true,
    "notes": "Our dispute table shows an active case for your Amazon transaction and that a provisional credit has already been issued while the investigation continues. Expected overall timelines remain: provisional credit (if eligible) within ~10 business days; investigation usually completes within ~45 days."
  },
  "sushi_kashiba_dispute": {
    "transaction_id": "txn_cfabb609133d",
    "dispute_record_found": false,
    "notes": "I could not find a dispute record for this transaction in the disputes table for your user profile. Possible reasons: the submission you made may still be propagating into our disputes system, or the dispute ID you received (dsp_d2b606a746e5) is not yet linked to the central disputes table I queried."
  },
  "next_steps_options": {
    "A_check_again_in_24-48_hours": "I can recheck the disputes table for dsp_d2b606a746e5 (Sushi Kashiba) in 24–48 hours and report back—useful if you think propagation delay is likely.",
    "B_escalate_reconciliation_now": "I can escalate this to the disputes team to reconcile the dispute IDs and confirm the Sushi Kashiba case is in our system (or create it if it didn’t propagate). This may require human handling—would you like me to do that?",
    "C_transfer_to_human_agent": "If you prefer immediate human assistance to reconcile the IDs and confirm provisional credits/status, I can transfer you to a human agent now."
  },
  "question": "Which option would you like me to take? Also — does the dsp_d2b606a746e5 confirmation you received include any submission timestamp or confirmation email that you can paste (optional)?"
}

{
  "message": "Done — I escalated and transferred this to our disputes/rewards reconciliation team with a detailed summary and request (reason: specialized_department_required). A human agent will take over and follow up on: linking the dispute IDs you received to your account, correcting the dispute reason to rewards undercredit, and confirming any provisional credits (and correcting them if needed).\n\nIs there anything else you’d like me to include in the escalation notes while you wait for the human agent?"
}
